task: frame-walk-end-to-end
agent: opus5-intent
started: 2026-09-05
branch: feature/frame-walk-end-to-end
worktree: ../okay-wt-walk

why: the consumer's third point, and the one I cannot argue with. Two
  of their defects today lived BETWEEN two correct code paths with 237
  unit tests green — a provider shown their OWN address back
  (contacts(viewer, other) called with a fixed direction), and a
  seeker told nothing at all because "the seeker got your contact" was
  a claim rather than a call. Neither is visible from any single seam,
  because neither is inside one.

  okay-frame and okay-intent have one caller and it is a classifier
  demo. A test that walks a whole exchange is worth more than another
  tier.

what: one test that goes message -> class -> frame -> extraction ->
  question -> answer -> assumption -> read-back -> ACT, through the
  real Conversation suspension and a real journal, with a restart in
  the middle, and asserts what a caller would actually do with the
  result — not that each piece works.

  It must be able to fail for the reason theirs did: an exchange that
  ends "complete" while the thing the caller needed was never
  produced.

files: okay-agent/src/test/scala/okay/agent/TestWalk.scala (new),
  specs/conversation.md, BACKLOG.md
